02eac"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"0e87d95f574bf8102b4674befd9b1294dbbfb60011334b2dd881632f0a24aba5","event_uuid":"26c965bb-588c-4d45-9e23-dc1f8531044d","position":{"commit_sha":"e8e8437fdadb9f0b8048f223362cfaec0444545e","position":"1792392920327184232-26c965bb-588c-4d45-9e23-dc1f8531044d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review 2026-10-19 (BLOCK, deterministic P11 ac-vagueness, no LLM findings): one AC item was flagged for subjective wording (\"client-appropriate default\", \"path-identical\", chained \"and\"). Description rewritten so each of the three criteria names the exact function, path, grep, build command, or tracker query that proves it, and each names the child story that delivers it. The config-seam story d279 is already certified at f147e08242f; this epic's certificate is the last gate before a lane can claim it.","timestamp":1792391276331306900},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Second plan review 2026-10-19 (BLOCK, 1 move), confirmed on f147e08242f: AC2's packaging predicate (`grep -c 'evals/'` over the wheel listing, `grep -c '/evals/'` over the sdist) could never print 0, because the wheel ships the whole `src/rebar` tree (`pyproject.toml:367`) including the Python package `rebar/llm/evals/`, and the sdist includes it too (`:398`). The patterns are now anchored to the archive root (`^evals/` after stripping the sdist's top directory), so only a top-level corpus directory matches. The AC also now states why the check exists: both build targets already exclude a top-level `evals/`, so it guards against a future include change rather than the current state.","timestamp":1792392568651111746}],"created_at":1788805607854735774,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0c61b8f7-0b89-466b-bc75-8a870799cb1c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"10ae-1ef7-97c9-4645"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nClient projects that supply their own criteria (`.rebar/criteria_routing.json`) must be able to run the same eval harnesses rebar uses for its core evals: plan replay, fixture mining, and provider parity. Today the harnesses hard-code repository paths under `docs/experiments/` and write into whatever checkout they are run from, the `evals` extra is unregistered, and 13 MB of executable research artefacts live under `docs/`. The operator ruled on 2026-09-06 that the hard-coded paths are a bug and the harnesses must be exposed to clients. Cites re-verified on origin/main f147e08242f.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar.llm.config.evals_corpus_root()` is the only place the replay cache, replay output, ledger, and project eval-spec roots are resolved: with no config it returns `<repo_root>/.rebar/evals`; with this repo's `rebar.toml` it returns `<repo_root>/docs/experiments` until the corpus move lands. `git grep -n 'docs/experiments' -- src/rebar/llm/evals` returns exactly one line, the `plan_replay/corpus.py:5` docstring. Checked by `tests/unit/evals/test_evals_corpus_root.py` (four precedence cases plus `test_no_hard_coded_roots`) and by `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_corpus.py` passing unchanged. Delivered by the config-seam story.\n- [ ] The research corpus (the `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/` tree) is moved to a top-level `evals/` directory, `rebar.toml` sets `corpus_root = \"evals\"`, and `git grep -n 'docs/experiments' -- src docs scripts tests .github` prints nothing. The top-level corpus is not shipped: after `python -m build`, `unzip -l dist/*.whl | awk '{print $4}' | grep -cE '^evals/'` prints `0` and `tar tzf dist/*.tar.gz | sed 's#^[^/]*/##' | grep -cE '^evals/'` prints `0` (both patterns are anchored to the archive root, so the shipped Python package `rebar/llm/evals/` does not match; `pyproject.toml:367` `packages = [\"src/rebar\"]` and `:398` sdist `include` already exclude a top-level `evals/`, so this check guards against a future include change). Checked by a repo-wide grep test and a packaging test. Delivered by the corpus-move story.\n- [ ] `docs/user-guide.md` gains one section, \"Running the eval harnesses in a client project\", whose three commands (plan replay, fixture mining, provider parity) each run to completion in a temp client repo after `rebar init` plus one `.rebar/evals/*.eval.yaml`; `pip install nava-rebar[evals]` is documented and `python -c \"from rebar._optional import EXTRAS; print('evals' in EXTRAS)\"` prints `True`; the 71 orphaned fixture-drift tasks (listed in this epic's first comment) are closed `obsolete` with the reason \"superseded by the client-runnable harness\". Checked by the docs gates in `make verify` and by `rebar search 'status:open fixture-drift'` returning 0 rows. Delivered by the client-documentation story.\n\n## Child decomposition\n- Config seam story (`disgusted-fretful-hare`, d279-4cf9-d1a6-4f7b): delivers criterion 1; plan-review certified.\n- Corpus move story: delivers criterion 2; depends on the config seam.\n- Client documentation story: delivers criterion 3; depends on the corpus move.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","10ae-1ef7-97c9-4645"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_id":"e47b-d3ef-338f-4bcd","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Expose the eval harnesses to client projects: configured corpus roots, no hard-coded repository paths, research corpus out of docs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0c61b8f7-0b89-466b-bc75-8a870799cb1c","63e362ba-6035-4436-a7ba-38362ccd6578","87ff2f5b-785e-4c2f-9f42-caf1390cd2df","afd6e792-f3cb-4b8d-8f65-49c69feb9827","42774c2a-b347-4b7d-a556-a3a07fd02eac","26c965bb-588c-4d45-9e23-dc1f8531044d","b0f52823-a495-4520-ade9-f71b1122584d","6e6f1cea-6a22-46a4-a5e9-f845c4012505","93f10ed9-3298-46a2-a95f-85b703e5f4b3","0839eaed-bc83-412b-bdc2-7a6ff2fb7e07","2a660231-ffe4-4b07-a0e4-f6e2af05d712"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792628786693212732,"uuid":"e9303156-7592-4a03-9409-429e0263698e"}